# Localhost after commands

Read **docs/LOCALHOST.md** for full setup (especially Cloud Agent vs laptop).

## Default port

Port order: `LOCAL_PORT` → `PORT` → **3000**. Active port is written to `.local-server.port` when started via `ensure-local` / `local-server.mjs`.

After running `npm run build`, `npm run verify`, `npm run qa`, or any command that changes the site bundle, confirm the local site is serving the latest build.

1. `postbuild` auto-runs `ensure-local` (restarts the local port after every local `npm run build`; skipped in CI).
2. If localhost is down or stale: `npm run ensure-local` or `LOCAL_PORT=3002 npm run ensure-local`
3. Full clean rebuild + browser: `npm run 67`
4. Print URL: `node scripts/print-local-url.mjs`
5. Verify: `curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://localhost:<port>/` (expect `200`). On Windows: `curl.exe` instead of `curl`.

If page is unstyled or chunks return 400: `rm -rf .next && npm run build`.

## Cloud Agent (critical)

HTTP 200 inside the VM does **not** mean the user can open `localhost` on their phone/laptop. Tell users to use **Cursor Desktop port forwarding** (Agents Window → plug icon), **remote desktop** on the agent, or **https://mobiledog-salon.com**. Do not leave the session with the VM server down after site-changing commands.
